# 1️⃣ Reverse a Linked List

## 📖 Problem

Reverse the given Linked List.

---

### Example

Before

```
10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → NULL
```

After

```
40 → 30 → 20 → 10 → NULL
```

---

### Approach

Maintain three pointers.

```
Previous

Current

Next
```

Move each pointer one step ahead.

---

### Visualization

```
NULL ← 10 ← 20 ← 30 ← 40
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* reverse(Node* head)
{
    Node* prev = NULL;
    Node* curr = head;

    while(curr != NULL)
    {
        Node* next = curr->next;

        curr->next = prev;

        prev = curr;

        curr = next;
    }

    return prev;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

### Space Complexity

```
O(1)
```

---

# 2️⃣ Find the Middle Node

## 📖 Problem

Find the middle node of a Linked List.

---

### Example

```
10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50
```

Middle

```
30
```

---

### Best Approach

Use two pointers.

```
Slow → moves one step

Fast → moves two steps
```

When Fast reaches the end,

Slow will be at the middle.

---

### Visualization

```
S

↓

10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → 50

↓

F
```

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
Node* middle(Node* head)
{
    Node* slow = head;
    Node* fast = head;

    while(fast && fast->next)
    {
        slow = slow->next;

        fast = fast->next->next;
    }

    return slow;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

---

# 3️⃣ Detect a Cycle

## 📖 Problem

Determine whether a Linked List contains a cycle.

---

### Example

```
10 → 20 → 30 → 40

      ↑       |

      |_______|
```

---

### Best Approach

Use Floyd's Cycle Detection Algorithm.

Also called

```
Tortoise and Hare Algorithm
```

---

### Logic

```
Slow → 1 step

Fast → 2 steps
```

If they meet,

Cycle exists.

---

### C++ Code

```cpp
bool hasCycle(Node* head)
{
    Node* slow = head;
    Node* fast = head;

    while(fast && fast->next)
    {
        slow = slow->next;

        fast = fast->next->next;

        if(slow == fast)
            return true;
    }

    return false;
}
```

---

### Time Complexity

```
O(n)
```

